{"title":"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, circumcircle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is drawn. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the incenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/a/ecad24a71ff166a321427f872f346a0d4c5f6dd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" /> be the intersection of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />-altitude and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/e/dde1774a06facbf7b3c05e82bc4ed9bd41cd786a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb1b7b0526168d6f1aa059eaabc8b9ec9a3421ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/ace7328133fbaac6396a6e5fc9fa65f335320cd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/8/2085f12278ac766ad8887ca2130847f0f4461734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AIH_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider a lineup of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> marbles, each colored black or white. Define the period of a lineup to be the smallest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that the lineup appears as a contiguous subsequence of an infinite repetition of a length-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> lineup. An ordering is called good if its period is at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The probability that a random lineup is good can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2><p>\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be an isosceles trapezoid such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/e/89ee5420004c3b2a8f1f0cf81594b54dbbb1da5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB\\parallel CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6bfa3da153ed5f2401dbc3f964ba7580b344c74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> as the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, respectively. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/8/5a8e84f08fc5577cd21e5b56c195303259eb6e34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC=36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/c/c3c20f7dcae373e27dcafa7c6c7b35b77b4516e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7ffcdfbb239f4fc6927d010456a569ad5d1ef307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />, the area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8adc7350215cb64aa533d094e40d69b4c4e1fc6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[AGF]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />. </p><center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d03c1440c939b4bb42b72056d0688f6975c10b1a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(10cm); fill((6,8/5)--(10,8/3)--(6,8)--cycle,lightgray); draw((0,0)--(36,0)--(30,8)--(6,8)--cycle); draw((6,8)--(12,0)--(0,0)); draw((0,0)--(30,8)); draw((6,8)--(6,0)); label(&quot;A&quot;, (6,8), NW); dot((6,8)); label(&quot;B&quot;, (30,8), NE); dot((30,8)); label(&quot;C&quot;, (36,0), SE); dot((36,0)); label(&quot;D&quot;, (0,0), SW); dot((0,0)); label(&quot;E&quot;,(12,0),S); dot((12,0)); label(&quot;M&quot;,(6,0),S); dot((6,0)); dot((6,8/5)); dot((10,8/3)); [/asy]\" width=\"475\" height=\"138\" /> </center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/756b0d6cfc1f3864b70941f8167538c6c7970a3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=2,b_0=3, a_n=\\left(a_{n-1}\\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"217\" height=\"23\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5dfb2ca3fef0f0c083777743e26d9312c4da4d55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n=\\left(b_{n-1}\\right)^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"23\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/3/c0347f07cfe011112f35133df69e8d06db1e04a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_n=a_n+b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"15\" />,. Find the last two digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/c/87c6ba6cb101c1a6bc760e7b6b875999049c1f62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1+c_2+\\dots+c_{2022}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2><p>\nConsider the following rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/dafb324902af9772751731e815ab84e05f4efcb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=8$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/6/4b67f8280b2f10bf75e16117010ba1e007a7b399.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CD=CT_2,\\quad 4T_2P_2=2DP_1=AC,\\quad[ADP_1C]=33, \\quad\\text{and}\\quad[ABP_2C]=34.\\]\" width=\"601\" height=\"18\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54b695d53cd6268d6f79728f8594fa3b9e81c9c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[P_1CP_2A]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />. </p><center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/d/a3d1ccf25f5af9862c9520d6e99bb1e35a27fd61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(6cm); dot((0,0)); dot((12,0)); dot((12,16)); dot((0,16)); draw((0,0)--(12,0)--(12,16)--(0,16)--(0,0)--cycle); dot((8,22)); dot((17,4)); dot((8,16)); dot((12,4)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (0,0), SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (12,0), SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (12,16), NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, (0,16), NW); label(&quot;$P_1$&quot;, (8,22), NE); label(&quot;$P_2$&quot;, (17,4), SE); label(&quot;$T_1$&quot;, (8,16), SE); label(&quot;$T_2$&quot;, (12,4), SW); draw((8,22)--(8,16),dashed+linewidth(.5)); draw((12,4)--(17,4),dashed+linewidth(.5)); [/asy]\" width=\"238\" height=\"285\" /> </center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be a positive integer, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be some variable. Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/1836e176638715dc6a5195645b5e71c4e527e797.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{x,a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"33\" height=\"19\" /> as the maximum fraction of elements in the set of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> natural numbers that may be contained in a subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> such that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is an element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/d/f4d0d7039a400779d0c3013db5ed5a4950068462.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ak$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> is not. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f192a11fdda4768a378f580013b7eeb607ed043.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{3,3}=\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" />, since we take the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/3/71350a031d3d4f8a3fdd44b2d1514a1557eff1ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> approaches infinity, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/1836e176638715dc6a5195645b5e71c4e527e797.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{x,a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"33\" height=\"19\" /> approaches a value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d874e17c7ea25b97dc858c88374b891b2a6f6d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />. The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e2d9c6c1d337e7453a077d240d0a8561c96962c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\prod_{i=2}^{100}P_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"45\" height=\"55\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/a/6faa52b65e38390e2f8c74d86b42da8932c0a69f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(2A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0ab21ac9dd166a23b8e00fe1ba1e72216e15b2ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(2B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a450e4c1c31ced46d7dcb853347426914bb9d9f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(2C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" /> be the not necessarily distinct roots of a monic cubic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33c22f5b4422c902ced564fd5847171f5cf5d8bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=\\frac{17}{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" />, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311d40edff75c2cd2562774cbcf1082202cdfaae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(A)\\sin(B)\\sin(C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/3/eb3bd49db3f0869867e44ebe0b5a0dd6c2a6294a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{m}}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"33\" height=\"39\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> squarefree. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A frog is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on a number line and wants to go to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. On each turn, if the frog is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the frog hops to one of the numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, inclusive, with equal probability (staying in place counts as a hop). It is then teleported to the largest multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that is less than or equal to the frog's position. The expected number of hops it takes for the frog to reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aeaa8a74c8fe8e5b89b7dfff5e8cbdd2996402a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> satisfy \\begin{align*} a^2+b^2&amp;=1,\\\\ x^2+y^2&amp;=1,\\quad\\text{and}\\\\ abxy-\\frac{1}{8}&amp;=b^2y^2. \\end{align*} find the sum of all distinct values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/7/56705b0a2a901109dadfc8eb37586a43fef4430a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b+x+y)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/48689d638ddca59030006d362cbd848607f63aa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p, q, r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" /> be the three roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/8/8b847e494e330ed8dd25827e7e72535e45c278f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3-2x^2-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" />. Find the value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a1d70a9d18eb652a7d108781ab95b078121559f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(p^3+qr)(q^3+pr)(r^3+pq).\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the number of solutions to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/0/e704994663fb1194654eb407eb8db0ef7a1eefec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3+36ab+64=27b^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is a real number, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/4/d146baeb4ee4a49b0a7cd395e126261db511693b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|b|\\le 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"62\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 11\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Regular pentagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> is inscribed in circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />are th with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66c98fae1403b2e04e000b76895df336b8522dde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> is the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> across <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f32db217d7630882c3441fa8821cd70a6958c3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be an intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1a61b7cccb5fc02c843c7b58e2d671c4c2c6d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DO}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />, and let line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> be the tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. The sum of the possible distances from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2f1dcbb9badfd3447d4e7351678b7d71ea9bff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\sqrt{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a squarefree positive integer. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 12\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In regular hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> with side length 1, an electron starts at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. When the electron hits an edge, it reflects off of it, with the angle of reflection equal to the angle of incidence. The electron first travels in a straight line to a point on edge <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. The electron bounces off of a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> edges before hitting a vertex. The electron stops and its total distance traveled is measured. The shortest possible distance the electron could have traveled can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/7/9c707f01031d7f0a1e7ec87f782a715b580482d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 13\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On a hot summer day, three little piggies decide to play with water balloons. The three piggies travel to a 200-floor parking garage each armed with exactly one water balloon. The game works as follows: \n</p>\n<ul><li>If a piggie drops a water balloon from any floor of the building, it will either break, or it will survive the fall.</li>\n<li>If the water balloon breaks, then any greater fall would have broken it as well.</li>\n<li>If the water balloon survives, then it would have survived any lesser fall.</li>\n<li>Every water balloon is identical and interchangeable.</li></ul>\n<p>The goal for the piggies is to find the lowest floor that will break a water balloon. Assuming they play optimally, what is the minimum number of tries in which they are guaranteed to find the lowest balloon-breaking floor?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 14\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider two externally tangent circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> with centers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee48e5d3968014ef1e27c31e56d2f7ea5f8cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> have radii of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. There exist points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef747a48a2a8d43c4841e12c89f2de2502a672e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/7/1375da8b94d688b4928311f04d35a57081ee0f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C, D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> are the external tangents of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />. The circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1c31c047878777dfc62f72efef75924195715d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BO_2D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at two points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/1/a6153b31b4bc98f72ed128a47fa0fd4b3563381a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX &lt; AY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" />. The length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/73205379672e860eb250c541187600fae3a3e225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/3/eb3bd49db3f0869867e44ebe0b5a0dd6c2a6294a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{m}}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"33\" height=\"39\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 15\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018064528\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.051 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.059 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 781/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 28063/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:24528:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018064528 and revision id 280160. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}